Statistical analysis

Unless specified otherwise, data is represented as the mean average of 3 independent experiments or more and
variation is shown by standard error of mean (s.e.m.). Statistically significant relationships were determined
using Student’s t-test or one-way analysis of variance (ANOVA), with a probability (p) value < 0.05 being the
statistical significance considered.

